# Customer exports (contain PII)
exports/

# Same rule, extended to the rest of experiments/. The -v2 directories above
# were already excluded on exactly this reasoning; these ones were simply never
# added, and they are 169 MB across 95 files. Every one is reproducible from the
# script sitting next to it (render.js, shots.js, outpaint.js, depth.py) — and
# unlike the -v2 dirs these mix source and output in one folder, so the rule has
# to be by extension rather than by directory.
#
# Committing a generated MP4 puts a permanent copy in history to save a command,
# and history is the one place a mistake cannot be tidied later without
# rewriting every clone.
experiments/**/*.mp4
experiments/**/*.jpg
experiments/**/*.jpeg
experiments/**/*.png
